diff --git a/docs/docker-32gb-rtx5090.md b/docs/docker-32gb-rtx5090.md
index f5f3f95..2ca9241 100644
--- a/docs/docker-32gb-rtx5090.md
+++ b/docs/docker-32gb-rtx5090.md
@@ -71,6 +71,67 @@ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/health
 - `PYTHONPATH=/workspace` — so the container uses the mounted repo (e.g. your branch).
 - `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True` — reduces fragmentation.
 
+**Step-by-step VRAM logging:** set `FISH_LOG_VRAM_STEPS=1` (e.g. in `docker run -e FISH_LOG_VRAM_STEPS=1`) to log `vram_step` at each pipeline stage (inference_start, ref_loaded, llama_queued, segment_decode_start/done, generate_long_start, after_prefill, after_first_stream_chunk, generate_long_done, inference_done). Grep logs for `vram_step` to see alloc_gb/max_gb per step and check if peak reaches 30+ GB.
+
+## Prometheus & Grafana
+
+The server exposes **Prometheus** metrics at **GET /metrics** (no auth). Use Prometheus to scrape this endpoint and Grafana to visualize.
+
+**Metrics:**
+
+| Metric | Type | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| `fish_speech_vram_allocated_gb` | Gauge | GPU memory allocated (GB) at last observation |
+| `fish_speech_vram_max_gb` | Gauge | Max GPU memory allocated (GB) since process start |
+| `fish_speech_tts_requests_total{streaming}` | Counter | Total TTS requests (streaming=true/false) |
+| `fish_speech_tts_request_duration_seconds{streaming}` | Histogram | Request duration |
+| `fish_speech_tts_ttfa_seconds{streaming}` | Histogram | Time to first audio segment (excl. WAV header) |
+| `fish_speech_prefill_seconds` | Histogram | Prefill (first token) duration |
+| `fish_speech_decode_one_token_seconds` | Histogram | Single-token decode duration |
+| `fish_speech_decode_n_tokens_seconds` | Histogram | Full decode_n_tokens duration (non-streaming path) |
+| `fish_speech_forward_fast_seconds` | Histogram | forward_generate_fast (one codebook) duration |
+| `fish_speech_model_params_gb{component}` | Gauge | Static weights (GB): llm_slow, llm_fast, dac |
+| `fish_speech_func_vram_delta_gb{func}` | Gauge | VRAM net change (GB) during last call (prefill, decode_n_tokens, dac_decode) |
+| `fish_speech_func_vram_peak_gb{func}` | Gauge | VRAM peak (GB) during last call |
+| `fish_speech_func_vram_intermediate_gb{func,point}` | Gauge | VRAM (GB) at intermediate point (e.g. decode_one_token_ar: after_slow_forward, after_fast_forward; dac: after_quantizer, after_decoder), running max per chunk |
+
+Values are updated at each pipeline step when `FISH_LOG_VRAM_STEPS=1`, and on every call to `/v1/debug/memory`. So with VRAM_STEPS=1 you see fine-grained curves during inference; or poll `/v1/debug/memory` (e.g. from a cron or script) to refresh gauges on an interval.
+
+**Optional:** `FISH_MEMORY_PROFILE=1` enables `torch.profiler.profile(profile_memory=True)` for one request in the worker; trace is exported to `results/memory_profile_<timestamp>.json` (open in Chrome Tracing or PyTorch Memory Viz for per-operator allocation).
+
+**Prometheus scrape** (add to `prometheus.yml` or your config):
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+  - job_name: fish-speech
+    static_configs:
+      - targets: ['host.docker.internal:8080']   # if Prometheus in Docker
+        # or: ['127.0.0.1:8080']                 # if Prometheus on host
+    scrape_interval: 5s
+```
+
+If the API server runs in Docker and Prometheus runs on the host, use the host’s IP or `host.docker.internal` and the published port (e.g. 8080).
+
+**Быстрый запуск Prometheus** (на хосте, пока API уже слушает 8080): создать `prometheus.yml` с блоком выше и запустить `prometheus --config.file=prometheus.yml` (или через Docker/пакет). Prometheus будет слушать порт 9090; в Grafana в качестве data source указывать именно его: `http://localhost:9090`.
+
+**Готовый стек (Prometheus + Grafana + дашборд):** из корня репо выполнить `docker compose -f examples/monitoring/docker-compose.yaml -p fish-monitoring up -d`. Grafana: http://localhost:3000, дашборд «Fish Speech TTS» подхватывается автоматически. Подробнее: `examples/monitoring/README.md`.
+
+**Как добавить в Grafana:** Grafana запрашивает метрики у **Prometheus** (у него есть API `/api/v1/query`), а не у нашего API-сервера. Наш сервер отдаёт только эндпоинт `/metrics` для **сбора** (scrape) Prometheus’ом.
+
+1. **Запустите Prometheus** и укажите в `prometheus.yml` job для Fish Speech (см. блок выше). Пример запуска на хосте: `prometheus --config.file=prometheus.yml` (по умолчанию слушает порт 9090).
+2. **В Grafana:** Connections → Data sources → Add data source → **Prometheus**.
+3. **URL** укажите адрес **Prometheus**, например `http://localhost:9090` (не `http://127.0.0.1:8080`). Сохраните (Save & test).
+4. В дашбордах используйте запросы к метрикам, например: `fish_speech_vram_allocated_gb`, `fish_speech_tts_requests_total`.
+
+Если Grafana в Docker на том же хосте, в поле URL используйте `http://host.docker.internal:9090` или IP хоста вместо `localhost`.
+
+**Grafana (панели):** Add Prometheus as a data source (URL e.g. `http://localhost:9090`). Example panels:
+
+- **Time series:** `fish_speech_vram_allocated_gb`, `fish_speech_vram_max_gb` (legend: “VRAM alloc”, “VRAM max”).
+- **Stat:** current `fish_speech_vram_max_gb` to see peak.
+
+Use a 5–15 s scrape interval to capture VRAM changes during short TTS requests.
+
